# hpuefi — HP's kernel module for hp-repsetup / hp-flash

Origin: HP softpaq **sp171387** "HP Flash and Replicated Setup Utilities for
Linux v3.26" (2026-01-15), file `non-rpms/hpuefi-mod-3.07.tgz`.
Download: https://ftp.hp.com/pub/softpaq/sp171001-171500/sp171387.tgz
(softpaq MD5 `1da80330f3697bbb4fcebbd5e06cabb4`).

## License

- **This kernel module is GPLv2** — the archive ships `COPYING` (GPL v2) and the
  source builds as a GPL module. It can be built and redistributed under GPL
  terms, which the tScrub image already honours for the kernel.
- The companion **binaries** (`hp-repsetup`, `hp-flash`) are NOT part of this
  directory; HP distributes them "as a courtesy, free of charge, AS-IS" with
  no warranty and no support (see the softpaq `README.txt`). Stage them with
  `stage-hp-tools.sh` — do not commit the binaries.

## Patches vs upstream (needed for the tScrub kernel, applied to hpuefi.c)

1. `MODULE_LICENSE("GPL")` added — upstream ships no license string and
   modpost refuses to build the module without one.
2. `vma->vm_flags |= VM_LOCKED` → `vm_flags_set(vma, VM_LOCKED)` (kernel 6.0+
   removed direct vm_flags assignment under mmap locking).
3. `hpuefi.h` is the **pre-rendered** header for the Buildroot kernel —
   upstream's `hpuefi-vm-flags.sh` reads `uname -r` off the *build host*,
   which is wrong for a cross build, so the generated header is checked in
   instead. Do NOT run `./hpuefi-vm-flags.sh` or plain `make` in this
   directory.

## Building

Do not build here by hand. `board/shredos/modules/build-into-overlay.sh` (run
from the Buildroot top directory) discovers this directory like every other
`modules/*/` and builds it with:

    make -C output/build/linux-6.18 M=<this dir> ARCH=x86_64 \
         CROSS_COMPILE=output/host/bin/x86_64-buildroot-linux-gnu- modules

The result lands in `usr/lib/modules/<kver>/extra/hpuefi.ko` in the overlay.

**Kernel bumps:** the module is vermagic-bound to the exact kernel build. A new
kernel without re-running the overlay build either fails to compile here (if
the 6.18-era API patches stop applying) or refuses to load (vermagic) — both
are loud. `build_tscrub.sh` on the build host already runs
`build-into-overlay.sh` as part of every image build.

## Runtime device node

The module registers character major `hpuefi` but does NOT create the node.
The appliance (Buildroot, no udev) creates it on demand — see
`product/src/37_hp_repsetup.sh` `hp_repsetup::_ensure_dev` (mknod with the
major from `/proc/devices`). `mkdevhpuefi` here is HP's equivalent one-liner,
kept for reference.

## Verified

Built and verified live on the Z840 bench (BIOS M60 v02.61) 2026-11-07:
settings dump, settings writes, and a full password set/clear round-trip all
work through this module + hp-repsetup. See
`research/hp-repsetup-integration/README.md`.
